<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDerivedNonCoherentUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has coherent derived unit" .
# 
# http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDerivedUnit
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDerivedUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDerivedUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDerivedUnit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\n  This property relates a system of units to a unit of measure that is defined within the system in terms\n   of the base units for the system. \n  That is, the derived unit is defined as a product of the base units for the system raised to some rational power.\n  " .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDerivedUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDerivedUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "derived unit" .
# 
# http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector
