# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topDataProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ApplicationMessage> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The MIME type of the Application Message content (e.g., 'application/json')."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Message Content Type"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The Content Type MUST be a UTF-8 Encoded String."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ApplicationMessage> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The character encoding or serialization used for the Application Message (e.g., 'UTF-8', 'Base64')."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Application Message encoding"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A UTF-8 Encoded String MUST NOT include an encoding of the null character U+0000."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageEncoding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The character data in a UTF-8 Encoded String MUST be well-formed UTF-8 as defined by the Unicode specification [Unicode] and restated in RFC 3629 [RFC3629]. In particular, the character data MUST NOT include encodings of code points between U+D800 and U+DFFF."@en .
