<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPacketIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A PUBLISH packet MUST NOT contain a Packet Identifier if its QoS value is set to 0."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPacketIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Each time a Client sends a new SUBSCRIBE, UNSUBSCRIBE,or PUBLISH (where QoS > 0) MQTT Control Packet it MUST assign it a non-zero Packet Identifier that is currently unused."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPacketIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Each time a Server sends a new PUBLISH (with QoS > 0) MQTT Control Packet it MUST assign it a non zero Packet Identifier that is currently unused."@en .
