<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Subscription Identifier Property. Variable Byte Integer (value > 0) identifying a subscription; returned in PUBLISH as applicable."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Subscription Identifier"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The Subscription Identifier can have the value of 1 to 268,435,455."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnackProperties> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Subscription Identifier Available Property in CONNACK. Byte 0/1 indicating support for Subscription Identifiers."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Subscription Identifier Available"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionIdentifierAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If present, this byte declares whether the Server supports Subscription Identifiers. A value is 0 means that Subscription Identifiers are not supported. A value of 1 means Subscription Identifiers are supported."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#SubscriptionEntry> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedByte> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Subscription Options byte for a Topic Filter in SUBSCRIBE. Encodes QoS, No Local, Retain As Published, and Retain Handling."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Subscription Option"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Bits 0 and 1 of the Subscription Options represent Maximum QoS field. This gives the maximum QoS level at which the Server can send Application Messages to the Client. It is a Protocol Error if the Maximum QoS field has the value 3."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Bits 0-1: Maximum QoS\r\n0 = QoS 0\r\n1 = QoS 1\r\n2 = QoS 2\r\n3 = Protocol Error\r\n\r\nBit 2: No Local\r\n0 = Forward messages normally\r\n1 = Do not forward messages from the same ClientID\r\n\r\nBit 3: Retain As Published\r\n0 = Forwarded messages have RETAIN set to 0\r\n1 = Forwarded messages keep the published RETAIN flag\r\n\r\nBits 4-5: Retain Handling\r\n0 = Send retained messages at the time of subscribe\r\n1 = Send retained messages only if the subscription does not already exist\r\n2 = Do not send retained messages at subscribe\r\n3 = Protocol Error\r\n\r\nBits 6-7: Reserved\r\nMust be 0; otherwise the SUBSCRIBE packet is malformed."@en .
