<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An observable quality (property, characteristic) of a FeatureOfInterest."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The height of a tree, the depth of a water body, or the temperature of a surface are examples of observable properties, while the value of a classic car is not (directly) observable but asserted."@en .
