<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Verifiable> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\n  An aspect class that holds properties that provide external knowledge and specifications of a given resource.\n  " .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Verifiable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Verifiable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Verifiable" .
# 
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/abbreviation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\n  <p>An abbreviation for a unit is a short ASCII string that is used in place of the full name for the unit in contexts where non-ASCII characters would be problematic,\n   or where using the abbreviation will enhance readability. \n  When a power of abase unit needs to be expressed, such as squares this can be done using abbreviations rather than symbols. \n  For example, <em>sq ft</em> means <em>square foot</em>, and <em>cu ft</em> means <em>cubic foot</em>.\n  </p>"^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/abbreviation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt> .
<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/abbreviation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "abbreviation" .
